# Client-reachable above-floor Web API calls that are genuinely safe.
#
# One `repo-relative/path.ts` per line, optionally `:<line>` to pin one site.
# `#` starts a comment.
#
# EMPTY ON PURPOSE. An entry here accepts a BLANK PAGE for anyone below the
# declared floor — the failure mode is the React error boundary, not a
# graceful degradation. Prefer one of:
#
#   - derive the value deterministically (what OPE-640 did — the random UUID
#     was also corrupting ICS identity, so the guard exposed a second bug)
#   - guard the call: `typeof x === "function"` or `x?.()` with a real fallback
#   - move the work to the server
#
# If you must add an entry, say which browsers it breaks and why that is
# acceptable, with an issue link.
